{"id":"42343339d913bb42","group":"58","path":"58/batch09/58-df-attaching-space.md","title":"Attaching Space","display":"df-attaching-space — Attaching Space","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-attaching-space","aliases":["58-df-attaching-space"],"display":"df-attaching-space — Attaching Space","depends_on":["[[58-df-zfc-set-disjoint-union.md]]","[[../batch15/58-df-zfc-rel-equivalence-closure-relation.md]]","[[../batch10/58-df-zfc-top2-quotient-topology.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-attaching-space"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-attaching-space</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-attaching-space — Attaching Space"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"6a42c12dd60b1f33\" href=\"?note=6a42c12dd60b1f33\" title=\"58-df-zfc-set-disjoint-union.md\">58-df-zfc-set-disjoint-union.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f719c6b47e823a62\" href=\"?note=f719c6b47e823a62\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-zfc-rel-equivalence-closure-relation.md\">../batch15/58-df-zfc-rel-equivalence-closure-relation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"fdeb0db348e01893\" href=\"?note=fdeb0db348e01893\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-zfc-top2-quotient-topology.md\">../batch10/58-df-zfc-top2-quotient-topology.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"b2e63b755a37f1dc\" href=\"?note=b2e63b755a37f1dc\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md\">../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"815e63e5071e7b58\" href=\"?note=815e63e5071e7b58\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Q,\\tau_Q,X,\\tau_X,Y,\\tau_Y,A,\\phi\\in V\">\\(Q,\\tau_Q,X,\\tau_X,Y,\\tau_Y,A,\\phi\\in V\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\subseteq Y\">\\(A\\subseteq Y\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(X,\\tau_X)\">\\(\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(X,\\tau_X)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(Y,\\tau_Y)\">\\(\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(Y,\\tau_Y)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"815e63e5071e7b58\" href=\"?note=815e63e5071e7b58\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcSetDisjointUnion}_S(D,X,Y)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcSetDisjointUnion}_S(D,X,Y)\\)</span> (tagged disjoint union, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"6a42c12dd60b1f33\" href=\"?note=6a42c12dd60b1f33\" title=\"58-df-zfc-set-disjoint-union.md\">58-df-zfc-set-disjoint-union.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S(\\phi,A,\\tau_A,X,\\tau_X)\">\\(\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S(\\phi,A,\\tau_A,X,\\tau_X)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"b2e63b755a37f1dc\" href=\"?note=b2e63b755a37f1dc\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md\">../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcRelEquivalenceClosureRelation}_S(E,R,D)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcRelEquivalenceClosureRelation}_S(E,R,D)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"f719c6b47e823a62\" href=\"?note=f719c6b47e823a62\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-zfc-rel-equivalence-closure-relation.md\">../batch15/58-df-zfc-rel-equivalence-closure-relation.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTop2QuotientTopology}_S(\\tau_Q,q,D,\\tau_D)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2QuotientTopology}_S(\\tau_Q,q,D,\\tau_D)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"fdeb0db348e01893\" href=\"?note=fdeb0db348e01893\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-zfc-top2-quotient-topology.md\">../batch10/58-df-zfc-top2-quotient-topology.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Attach}_S\\subseteq V^8\">\\(\\mathrm{Attach}_S\\subseteq V^8\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{df\\text{-}attaching\\text{-}space}\\vdash{}&amp;\\mathrm{Attach}_S(Q,\\tau_Q,X,\\tau_X,Y,\\tau_Y,A,\\phi)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;A\\subseteq Y\\land\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(X,\\tau_X)\\land\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(Y,\\tau_Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\exists D,\\tau_D,\\tau_A,R,E,q\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{ZfcSetDisjointUnion}_S(D,X,Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\tau_D=\\{W\\subseteq D:\\{x\\in X:\\langle0,x\\rangle\\in W\\}\\in\\tau_X\\land\\{y\\in Y:\\langle1,y\\rangle\\in W\\}\\in\\tau_Y\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\tau_A=\\{U\\cap A:U\\in\\tau_Y\\}\\land\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S(\\phi,A,\\tau_A,X,\\tau_X)\\\\\n&amp;\\land R=\\{\\langle\\langle1,a\\rangle,\\langle0,\\phi(a)\\rangle\\rangle:a\\in A\\}\\land\\mathrm{ZfcRelEquivalenceClosureRelation}_S(E,R,D)\\\\\n&amp;\\land Q=\\{[d]_E:d\\in D\\}\\land q=\\{\\langle d,[d]_E\\rangle:d\\in D\\}\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop2QuotientTopology}_S(\\tau_Q,q,D,\\tau_D)\\Bigr).\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{df\\text{-}attaching\\text{-}space}\\vdash{}&amp;\\mathrm{Attach}_S(Q,\\tau_Q,X,\\tau_X,Y,\\tau_Y,A,\\phi)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;A\\subseteq Y\\land\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(X,\\tau_X)\\land\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(Y,\\tau_Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\exists D,\\tau_D,\\tau_A,R,E,q\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{ZfcSetDisjointUnion}_S(D,X,Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\tau_D=\\{W\\subseteq D:\\{x\\in X:\\langle0,x\\rangle\\in W\\}\\in\\tau_X\\land\\{y\\in Y:\\langle1,y\\rangle\\in W\\}\\in\\tau_Y\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\tau_A=\\{U\\cap A:U\\in\\tau_Y\\}\\land\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S(\\phi,A,\\tau_A,X,\\tau_X)\\\\\n&amp;\\land R=\\{\\langle\\langle1,a\\rangle,\\langle0,\\phi(a)\\rangle\\rangle:a\\in A\\}\\land\\mathrm{ZfcRelEquivalenceClosureRelation}_S(E,R,D)\\\\\n&amp;\\land Q=\\{[d]_E:d\\in D\\}\\land q=\\{\\langle d,[d]_E\\rangle:d\\in D\\}\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop2QuotientTopology}_S(\\tau_Q,q,D,\\tau_D)\\Bigr).\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The tagged union prevents accidental identifications before quotienting; the least equivalence relation then identifies each <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle1,a\\rangle\">\\(\\langle1,a\\rangle\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle0,\\phi(a)\\rangle\">\\(\\langle0,\\phi(a)\\rangle\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The result records both the quotient carrier <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Q\">\\(Q\\)</span> and its quotient topology <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_Q\">\\(\\tau_Q\\)</span>; continuity uses the subspace topology <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_A\">\\(\\tau_A\\)</span> induced from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_Y\">\\(\\tau_Y\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-zfc-set-disjoint-union.md","status":"resolved","id":"6a42c12dd60b1f33","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-set-disjoint-union.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-zfc-rel-equivalence-closure-r